// Abyss Enemies
AdultEidolonWyrm: Colossal creatures lurking within the void of the deepest layer of the Abyss.
Bloatfish: Large fish which can easily resist the crushing pressure of the depths and any efforts to pierce their skin.
BobbitWorm: An ambush predator that lurks within the deepest parts of the abyss, it extends out rapidly to snatch unsuspecting prey.
BoxJellyfish: These jellyfish unique for their cube-like shape act like ambush predators, waiting for something edible to approach them to then hastily swim towards prey in an effort to consume it.
ChaoticPuffer: While it behaves like a regular pufferfish for the most part, once destroyed its water reserves will be expelled at extreme temperatures, severely burning anything in its proximity.
ColossalSquid: Squid that have grown to monstrous sizes, these are one of the apex predators of the abyssal depths.
Cuttlefish: Despite the cuddly appearance, these squid-like creatures prove capable ambush predators.
Devilfish: Named as such for their mask, they remain docile until their mask breaks.
EidolonWyrm: Little is known about these enigmatic creatures.
GiantSquid: squee
GulperEel: A massive eel that resides within the deeper levels of the abyss; Its jaws can extend to an unnatural degree which allows it to swallow prey completely unnoticed.
LaserFish: This fish has a symbiotic relationship with bacteria that gather in large sacs on its head, though they blind it, these bacteria release deadly blasts to clear its path and harm any potential predators.
LuminousCorvina: This creature's survival methods are unusual, yet clever: Once a potential threat is near it, it will release a shrill pulse, alerting all other creatures of a potential meal's location... While it remains unscathed.
MirageJelly: These jellyfish create illusions of themselves to confuse both predator and prey.
MorayEel: These eels prefer to remain hidden within underwater structures, only ocassionally roaming open water.
Oarfish: These colossal fish live in deep sea to avoid turbulent waters, and are likely the source for many myths.
ReaperShark: pushups, situps, and plenty of juice
ToxicMinnow: Perhaps in a strange bid from evolution, these fish will process toxic chemicals from the plants they eat and store them as a self defense mechanism... however, it's only released on death, rendering it moot.
Viperfish: Initially docile fish, they rest firmly almost at the bottom of the food chain, but will react once they feel threatened.
// Acid Rain Enemies
AcidEel: Their dorsal fin allows great movement underwater, which allows them to rush towards prey.
Bloodworm: An unnaturally large worm... and a great feast for any fish mad or wise enough to go for it.
FlakBaby: Much like other young creatures, they tend to imprint easily to the first large creature they see.
FlakCrab: It would be a regular crab if it weren't for its unusual shell, through which it can expel corrosive water at high speed.
GammaSlime: The slimes in the region grow more powerful as the sea's condition worsens more and more.
IrradiatedSlime: This slime has been irradiated! Best not to approach it.
NuclearToad: When threatened, they burst in an attempt to save the rest of their species.
Orthocera: A creature thought extinct, yet somehow thriving in the sulphurous sea. You have to wonder what other secrets these waters hold.
Radiator: It ingests the potent toxins found in its home and displays them on its back, touching them would be a bad idea.
Skyfin: Likely flying fish that adapted to their harsh conditions.
SulfurousSkater: These creatures are capable of remaining on the surface of the water, barely noticeable, they're also capable of flight if they need to.
Trilobite: An example of an ancient creature persisting in the sulphurous sea, they have remarkable strength to be able to fling themselves, yet weigh as much as they do.
WaterLeech: They eagerly swim to any prey they can find thanks to their great sense of smell, sucking the blood out of their host and at once also injecting venom onto them.
// Astral Enemies
Aries: These creatures hop and chase any threat to the infection relentlessly.
AstralProbe: Once a common bird, its only purpose now is to defend the infection.
AstralSlime: A slime covered in the infection's essence, it reflects the cosmos above...
Astralachnea: Once regular cave spiders, they have been reduced down to mere sentries for the infection.
BigSightseer: These flying abominations produce a chemical within their shells that's then spat out onto its enemies.
FusionFeeder: These sand sharks have been completely overriden with the infection's knowledge, and what was once hunger has become thirst for distant stars.
Hadarian: These creatures possess extremely tough membranes in their wings, allowing them to apply pressure on their enemies even if there's counterattack.
Hive: An amalgamation of creatures, these hives will split off small chunks of themselves to attack enemies.
Hiveling: One sample of a piece of Hive, these can be very threatening in large numbers.
Mantis: A swift, nimble creature capable of traversing most terrain thanks to its many legs. It releases high speed scythes by swinging its claws.
Nova: Simple creatures lacking in means of offense or defense, instead they charge at enemies and self destruct in order to defend the infection.
SmallSightseer: Smaller variants of sightseers, these lack the ability to spit deadly chemicals, and instead charge at their enemies, much like they once did as Demon Eyes.
StellarCulex: On its face reside multiple pincers they use as weapons to subdue organic creatures.
Twinkler: A rare case of the infection creating a docile creature, it makes excellent bait as it flickers vividly.
// Brimstone Crags Enemies
CalamityEye: what a calamity
CharredSlime: A slime infused with Charred Ore, it's a perfect match!
CultistAssassin: A devotee brought to madness by the power of the brimstone flame.
DespairStone: A construct made from Brimstone Slag, it's said that its volatile movements are the result of the souls it contains fighting to get out.
Scryllar: The twisted remains of explorers who attempted to harvest the crags' remains.
SoulSlurper: Guardians of the crags, they relentlessly chase potential threats to their home.
// Normal Uncategorized Enemies
AeroSlime: The essence of Aerialite Ore has allowed this slime to take to the skies!
AngryDog: very angy boi
ArmoredDigger: A mechanical worm constructed by Draedon for the purposes of extracting resources... but it's been abandoned.
BlightedEye: An eye with similar behaviour to the Demon Eye.
BloomSlime: A slime infused with Uelibloom Ore, it's almost indistinguishable!
Bohldohr: He is here.
Cnidrion: Enigmatic creatures from the desert that store massive amounts of water within their bodies... is there's something more to them?
CosmicElemental: A strange creature that wanders the caves of the world, even stranger are the trinkets it sometimes holds!
CrawlerAmber: A scaredy lizard from the underground covered in Amber, when threatened it will do its best to run away!
CrawlerAmethyst: A scaredy lizard from the underground covered in Amethyst, when threatened it will do its best to run away!
CrawlerCrystal: A scaredy lizard from the underground covered in Crystals, when threatened it will do its best to run away!
CrawlerDiamond: A scaredy lizard from the underground covered in Diamonds, when threatened it will do its best to run away!
CrawlerEmerald: A scaredy lizard from the underground covered in Emeralds, when threatened it will do its best to run away!
CrawlerRuby: A scaredy lizard from the underground covered in Rubies, when threatened it will do its best to run away!
CrawlerSapphire: A scaredy lizard from the underground covered in Sapphires, when threatened it will do its best to run away!
CrawlerTopaz: A scaredy lizard from the underground covered in Topazes, when threatened it will do its best to run away!
CrimulanBlightSlime: A slime blessed by a higher being, and one of the few of its kind not to consume for itself.
CryoSlime: A slime infused with Cryonic Ore, its crystal spikes look dangerous...
Cryon: Ice constructs with runes inscribed on their heads... Who made them?
EbonianBlightSlime: A slime blessed by a higher being, and one of the few of its kind not to consume for itself.
Eidolist: A cultist that succumbed to their cult magicks, yet still, they seem to guard something...
FearlessGoldfishWarrior: This brave fish sets out for glorious battle and adventure, equipped with the finest gear the land has to offer!
Frogfish: It's a frog! It's a fish! It's superfish!... not really.
HeatSpirit: Once a human that lost their mind to the crags, now it seeks to eliminate any signs of foreign life within its new home.
Horse: A man-made elemental run with clockwork mechanisms, records say its previous design resembled a horse.
IceClasper: Skilled hunters that know no bound when hunting prey.
ImpiousImmolator: Initially passive burning spirits, they roam the lands peacefully, until something impedes them.
MantisShrimp: These shrimp possess one of the deadliest punches in nature, rivalling the strength of a bullet, and easily breaking sturdy shells.
OverloadedSoldier: The corpse of a soldier supercharged with Phantoplasm, then reanimated by vengeful spirits.
PerennialSlime: A slime infused with Perennial Ore so heavily that a flower has grown on it, how pretty!
PhantomDebris: We're not doing this again.
PhantomSpirit: One of many spirits imprisoned within the dungeon, while not quite as strong as the others, it's still dangerous to fight.
PhantomSpiritL: One of many spirits imprisoned within the dungeon, the ages spent imprisoned have led it to madness.
PhantomSpiritM: One of many spirits imprisoned within the dungeon, an everlasting burning hatred for its jailor fuels it.
PhantomSpiritS: One of many spirits imprisoned within the dungeon, its prolonged torment has left it in eternal sadness.
Piggy: oink!
Pitbull: Rabid, dangerous and uncontrolled dogs that roam unseen in the night.
ProfanedEnergy: A living altar. Its flame burns fiercely to aid its master.
SandTortoise: Like their jungle and tundra cousins, they prove quite the serious threat with their high speed lunges.
ScornEater: The strongest of Providence's regular followers, they make any unfaithful being pray.
SeaUrchin: A spiny animal native to the ocean that flings itself around relentlessly in defense of its territory, though mostly helpless when outside water, given enough time they can make it back home.
ShockstormShuttle: A small scouter saucer from a distant civilization, yet still very aggressive. Hopefully the rest of them aren't like that!
StormlionCharger: This variant of antlion is very unusual with its feeding; As it takes to the surface and reaches upwards with its mandibles to act as lightning rods, feeding off the storms' lightning.
SunBat: A light in the dark.
Sunskater: sunfish gang
CloudElemental: Once a revered deity, she remains angry at the world and the people which abandoned her.
WulfrumDrone: A strange little mechanism of unknown origin, they try to keep away intruders from their territory by swooping down at them.
WulfrumGyrator: A metal orb made of wulfrum, they fling themselves at their enemies to attack.
WulfrumHovercraft: These machines travel via propulsion, hovering over the lands. They seek out trespassers, even if their analysis might be inaccurate in the current day.
WulfrumPylon: These pyramid shaped machines help their allies by empowering them if they're in their protective force-field.
WulfrumRover: A small machine of unknown origin, they roam the lands with great duty and curiosity.
WulfrumSlime: you shouldn't even be here you know
// Plague Enemies
PlagueBee: A bee overtaken by plague nanomachines, it now serves the plague completely.
PlagueBeeLarge: A large bee overtaken by plague nanomachines, it now serves the plague completely.
PlaguedDerpling: A derpling overtaken by plague nanomachines, its limbs have come off, now flying instead to infect more of the jungle.
PlaguedFlyingFox: A flying fox overtaken by plague nanomachines, deadly plague oozes from its mouth.
PlaguedJungleSlime: A slime taken over by the plague nanomachines... Yet, in its slimy wisdom, it behaves the same.
PlaguedTortoise: A tortoise overtaken by plague nanomachines, its shell now shines bright silver.
// Sulphur Sea Enemies
Catfish: These fish use their whiskers to find their way and catch prey.
AnthozoanCrab: A strong, territorial crab that hurls boulders to anything that approaches its territory.
BelchingCoral: doot!
Flounder: Relatively simple fish that launch acid towards their prey in order to subdue it.
Gnasher: A turtle covered by debris and waste from the sulphurous waters it inhabits. Be careful not to approach it, its jaw strength is quite potent for a creature its size.
Mauler: This shark has adapted well to the sulphurous sea, and is uncontested as an apex predator of its habitat.
Trasher: Despite their ferocious appearance and great jaw, these crocodiles prefer to scavenge for food and leftovers.
// Sunken Sea Enemies
BlindedAngler: An angler which uses primitive electroception to hunt prey.
Clam: Regular mollusks that behave like any other.
EutrophicRay: A stingray that spends most of its time as a docile creature, but that will release its energy reserves as short bursts of speed when threatened.
GhostBell: Electric jellyfish that drift gently in the sunken sea, their bodies are charged with electricity.
GhostBellSmall: Like their adult counterparts, they drift gently. Be careful not to hurt them!
PrismTurtle: Slow swimmers that occasionally wander to the surface of their habitat to lay eggs.
SeaFloaty: Strange creatures that hide upon sight of a predator.
SeaMinnow: These small fish lay at the bottom of the food chain, but also make up most of the sunken sea's population; They feed on whatever scraps fall from the desert above.
SeaSerpent: Mostly passive eels that drift along the still waters, if angered however, they prove quite the stubborn attackers!
// Town NPCs
Bandit: A slick and capable thief that prefers keeping fights at a distance.
DrunkPrincess: The Creator
Permafrost: Despite his age, he's still a real cool guy.
SeaKing: A King displaced from his realm; He knows his tragedy, but has come to peace with it.
// Boss Minions
AquaticParasite: Small yet agile creatures, these creatures can leap out of the water to reach their prey.
AquaticSeeker: A peculiar creature similar in appearance to the Aquatic Scourge. These creatures soar far across sky and ocean in search of food.
AquaticUrchin: A spiny animal native to the ocean that flings itself around relentlessly in defense of its territory, though mostly helpless when outside water, given enough time they can make it back home.
Brimling: Extensions of the Brimstone Elementals, they possess no mind, and simply serve as additional weapons for the elemental.
LifeSeeker: Sentries for the clone, their lasers prove deadly.
SoulSeeker: Guardians for the clone, they could be empowered Soul Slurpers.
DarkEnergy: A rift in time and space created by Ceaseless Void.
Cryocore: A servant of the Ice Fortress.
IceMass: The souls of those who passed away in the deadly tundra, they now seek to freeze others and doom them to a similar fate.
DesertScourgeSmall: The Desert Scourge's children. They swarm and tear prey in seconds, and hunt alongside their parent.
DriedSeeker: A small sea serpent that suffered much the same fate as the Desert Scourge, it serves as a companion in its endless search for food.
CosmicGuardian: His right hand man, it will spring into action once the Devourer feels threatened.
DankCreeper: Guardians of the filthy mind.
DarkHeart: It's filled with stagnant corruption water that leaks as it flies overhead, any organic matter that comes into contact with that water is slowly corroded.
HiveBlob: A ball of flesh and rotting matter, flung out by its master as fodder.
HiveCyst: The result of many corrupted beings fused together, destroying it would be a terrible mistake.
LeviathanStart: A mysterious being... perhaps it's hiding something?
AquaticAberration: This creature devours whole schools of fish entirely by itself.
Parasea: These strange serpents are some of the Leviathan's spawn.
CosmicLantern: These lanterns rarely see use in combat, and instead allow their user to see through any form of darkness.
Sepulcher: A mechanical abomination summoned by the Brimstone Witch. Its armor proves unbreakable.
SoulSeekerSupreme: A construct of the witch, it and its brethren serve as a shield when a battle proves difficult.
// Bosses
AquaticScourge: A distant relative of the Desert Scourge, its appearance has been changed heavily by the sulphurous waters; Due to the ample food supply and its adaptions to its environment, it's far less aggressive than its kin.
AstrumAureus: One of Draedon's machines, even it succumbed to the infection's spread.
AstrumDeus: After its catastrophic fall to the infection and subsequent demolition by an upstart worm, it seeks to return to the cosmos.
BrimstoneElemental: Once a great goddess, all she has within her heart now is hate. Hate for all that might pity her.
Dragonfolly: Failed clones of the Tyrant's loyal dragon, they were released onto the wild on accident, now roaming the jungle unopposed.
Catastrophe: One of the clone's creations, and a recreation of the Witch's brother Catastrophe. It possesses no will of its own.
Cataclysm: One of the clone's creations, and a recreation of the Witch's brother Cataclysm. It possesses no will of its own.
Calamitas: A failed clone of the Brimstone Witch contained within a metallic vessel, she wanders the night with seemingly little purpose.
CeaselessVoid: Created after a failed experiment with the Devourer of Gods' dimension hopping ability, this being desires nothing more than to consume all the life force it can.
Crabulon: Once an ocean crab that migrated towards the underground caves that resembled its home the most... It met an unfortunate fate, now a walking puppet of the shrooms.
Cryogen: An ice cage few have seen in the harshest blizzards, its presence causes an aurora to form in the sky.
DesertScourge: Once a great sea worm, it's been reduced to a husk, desperately searching meals to devour on a regular basis.
DevourerofGods: Long live the purple worm!
HiveMind: The master of the corruption, it serves as the corruption's greatest offensive asset.
Leviathan: Theorized to be the very last of her kind, this reptile only awakens if her slumber is disturbed.
Anahita: This elemental was known for her immense power and mastery of water in her home. But that was long ago.
OldDuke: The apex predator of the sulphurous sea. It doesn't seem native to the polluted sea, and it's shockingly strong for its apparent age.
PerforatorSmall: The smallest of the perforators, its purpose is to pierce.
PerforatorMedium: The middest of the perforators, its purpose is to tear.
PerforatorLarge: The largest of the perforators, its purpose is to devour.
PerforatorCyst: The culmination of the crimson's horrific flesh, avoid it at all costs.
PerforatorHive: Birthed in the crimson, though unknown if it's a servant of it, as its worms tear through the crimson flesh regularly.
PlaguebringerGoliath: A queen bee that has fallen victim to the plague, now it carries out its directives as its strongest soldier.
Polterghast: The culmination of anger and hatred, as the vengeful spirits have coalesced into a singular monster with one objective: to kill the man responsible for their endless suffering.
ProfanedGuardian: mr. donut one, he stabs real good
ProfanedGuardian2: mr. donut two, he exists real good
ProfanedGuardian3: mr. donut three, we already did this joke
Providence: Born from dark and light, Providence seeks to cleanse all from desire with the might of her Holy Flame.
Ravager: The innumerable corpses of the undead, forced to rise once more in a bid for victory... A great mistake that cost its creators their lives.
Signus: A strange figure draped in dark robes and even darker history...
EbonianSlimeGod: The core's corrupted right hand man, or in this case, slime.
CrimulanSlimeGod: The core's crimson right hand man, or in this case, slime.
SlimeGodCore: One of the oldest creatures in the world, and a god revered by Statis' clan.
StormWeaver: One of the Devourer's sentinels, still young and inexperienced.. Should the day arrive where its power rivals the Devourer's, he will surely make quick work of it.
SupremeCalamitas: The Witch herself in the flesh. Her brimstone magic is not something to be taken lightly.
SupremeCataclysm: The Witch's revived brother, Cataclysm. He is a shell of his former self however.
SupremeCatastrophe: The Witch's revived brother, Catastrophe. He is a shell of his former self however.
Yharon: The tyrant's loyal lifelong friend has set his sight on you.
// Minibosses
CragmawMire: A slime that against all odds developed a calcified shell.
GiantClam: An oversized clam large enough to trap a person within it. It might make a good shield, who knows?
GreatSandShark: Even in a foreign environment, these persistent sharks have managed to thrive and made themselves a comfortable home.
NuclearTerror: A terrifyingly powerful creature that only makes itself known once the worst has come.
PlaguebringerShade: What would have been a queen bee, taken away by the plague, now only serving as one of its many servants.
